  closer to Beck wrecking his drones and  using his spider sense to blast through  the illusions that barf tech throws up  he also defends himself against a hail  of bullets that Mysterio fires at him  one of which strikes Mysterio himself  apparently fatally but of course  considering the scale of vex illusions  it's impossible not to wonder if he's  actually a goner there's plenty of  evidence from the comics to make this a  legitimate question not only has Quentin  Beck faked his own death before but  several other criminals have taken on  the identity of Mysterio in Beck's place  in short there's plenty of room for the  master of illusion to make a return one  way or another and either way  unbeknownst to Peter Mysterio's back-up  plan is now in motion after Spidey hulks  the attack one of the people on  Mysterio's payroll can be seen  downloading data onto a portable drive  walking away with unknown intentions  it's implied that what's been copied as  data related to the fight specifically  camera footage from the drones it ends  up coming back in a big way during the  mid credit scene but for all anyone  knows in the hours after the battle  Mysterio has been defeated and the  threat he poses is over unfortunately  poor Peter Parker is far from done with  this fight suffice to say it looks like  this Peter can't even get through high  school with a secret identity intact if  only he had gone into the battle dressed  as night monkey this probably wouldn't  have been such a big deal  the comics once again offers some  precedent for these plot points back in  Mysterio's first appearance an amazing  spider-man number 13 he poses as a crime  fighter and strikes a deal with Jay  jonah Jameson to expose Spidey's  identity to the world and the pages of  The Daily Bugle what we see in the mid  credit scene is a clear reference to  Mysterio's debut before all of that goes  down Peter returns to New York having  finally established a romantic  relationship with MJ that's 